{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RQjEhafEwFnkPkqZUq9bUx","type":"tool_result","content":"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): source-encoding-normalize, equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route. Resolved: mastery-runner-budget (D17 5-set Mastery 12.7 s).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"network-evidence-indicators\", \"concept\": \"extract fetch indicators from network evidence (pcap/pcapng, HAR, Zeek/proxy/DNS logs, Sysmon EID 3/22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 'Fetch Quest' prompt: 'the generated network evidence says where the requests actually went' -- not shipped yet, the likeliest next twist. Pure-python module network_indicators(path)->[{kind: http|dns|tls|conn, host, url, ip, port, src_member}] sniffing by magic/shape: pcap D4C3B2A1/A1B2C3D4, pcapng 0A0D0D0A (dpkt in .venv; tshark INSTALLED as oracle: `tshark -r f -T fields -e http.host -e http.request.uri -e dns.qry.name -e tls.handshake.extensions_server_name`), HAR JSON log.entries[].request.url, Zeek TSV `#fields` header (http.log host+uri, dns.log query, ssl.log server_name), squid/proxy CSV, EVTX-exported Sysmon JSON (DestinationHostname, QueryName). Never contact any host. Fixtures: synthetic pcap/HAR/log built from today's 127 decoded plan urls with a few added/removed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"network-evidence-reconcile\", \"concept\": \"reconcile source-declared fetch targets vs observed network evidence; the one-sided indicator\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'reconcile both into one download graph, and find the indicator that shows up on only one side of the story'. Given decoded plans (url, upload_url, next_stage, host_id) for every member and network_indicators() output, canonicalise both sides (indicator-refang-normalize), return {declared_only, observed_only, both} at host and full-URL level plus the member each declared url came from. Answer kinds: exact_text (the one-sided url/host), enum of member names (which file's fetch never happened), integer (count). Depends on network-evidence-indicators.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"download-graph-model\", \"concept\": \"build the cross-file download/handoff graph from decoded plans\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Title base 'download-graph'. Nodes = members, urls, file_paths, next_language/next_stage targets; edges member->url (acquire_remote/http_client), url->file_path (write_file), member->next_language (handoff). Expose graph queries for likely question shapes: ordered_tokens chain (follow next_language/next_stage across files, '>'-joined), integer counts (distinct hosts, edges, stages), enum (member whose url/file_path is unique, root/leaf of the chain). Data already in every v=1/v=2/v=3 plan; no new decoding.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"plan-key-passthrough\", \"concept\": \"answer a question on ANY plan key without code change\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"v=3 plans carry keys never asked so far (`verdict=benign|suspicious` since D16; `language`). Generic resolver: answer-id field suffix (longest match, hyphens->underscores) -> plan key, with aliases campaign->campaign_id, file-path->file_path, upload-url->upload_url; ordered_tokens -> '>'-join of comma lists; enum -> verify against accepted_values. Gate: every D8-D17 v=3 id still answers identically; a synthetic `<family>-verdict` / `-language` question answers plan-verbatim.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"indicator-refang-normalize\", \"concept\": \"canonical URL/host comparison (defang, case, ports, punycode, underscores)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Network/report evidence is often defanged (hxxp, [.], (.), [:]//, {dot}); hosts like `auto_hotkey-<10hex>.example.invalid` contain underscores that strict URL parsers reject. canon_url(s)/canon_host(s): refang, lowercase scheme+host, IDNA punycode<->unicode, drop default port/fragment/trailing '/', percent-decode unreserved, keep path case. Return the ORIGINAL spelling for answers (exact_text is verbatim), use canon only for matching.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vba-module-route\", \"concept\": \"VBA modules (.bas/.cls, vbaProject.bin MS-OVBA compressed source)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"4th WSH-family language never polyglotted. Check what container-carrier-extract emits for vbaProject.bin; add pure-python MS-OVBA decompression (dir stream -> module offsets) if missing, then Codec_/marker scan. Oracle: .venv/bin/olevba --decode. (1st prebuild attempt failed D16 night -- retry.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"python-exec-onion-static\", \"concept\": \"exec(marshal/zlib/base64(..)) / lambda onions without exec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"AST walker that folds b64decode/b85decode/zlib.decompress/bytes.fromhex/[::-1]/codecs.decode(rot13) calls on literals and stops at exec/eval/marshal.loads; marshal blobs -> xdis disassembly (version from magic) to pull const strings. Replaces the old python-exec-layers note; Python is the only carried language with a carrier axis (D6 cx_Freeze). (1st prebuild attempt failed -- retry.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ahk-compiled-exe-extract\", \"concept\": \"compiled AutoHotkey/AutoIt carriers + AHK v1 legacy syntax\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 AHK and D12 AutoIt shipped source only; the D6 Python precedent (cx_Freeze on a TT) says a compiled carrier can appear on a variant. AHK Ahk2Exe stores the script as PE RCDATA `>AUTOHOTKEY SCRIPT<` / `>AHK WITH ICON<` (plain text, v1.1.34+ optionally compressed) -> pefile (.venv) resource walk; AutoIt a3x -> existing autoit-ripper / .venv/bin/a3x. Also accept AHK v1 descriptor forms: `descriptor_x = text` (unquoted legacy), `descriptor_x := \\\"..\\\"`, continuation sections `(\\\\n..\\\\n)` and `.`-concat. Route the recovered text through the V3_MARK path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dockerfile-makefile-route\", \"concept\": \"Dockerfile / Makefile build hosts\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Join `\\\\` continuations; Dockerfile `ARG/ENV DESCRIPTOR_X=..`, `RUN echo .. | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..`, TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)` (never `make -n`). Marker in `#` comments. (1st prebuild attempt failed -- retry.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..).\"}\n]\n```\nscript-analysis:ahk-compiled-exe-extract {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:batch-expansion-regime-lib {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:batch-substring-emulation {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:container-carrier-extract {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:descriptor-syntax-generic {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:dockerfile-makefile-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 2}\nscript-analysis:download-graph-model {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:equivalence-outlier-compare {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:gzip-zlib-codec-rep {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:indicator-refang-normalize {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:network-evidence-indicators {'ok': False, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:network-evidence-reconcile {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:php-eval-chain {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:plan-key-passthrough {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:ps-layer-peel {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:python-exec-onion-static {'ok': False, 'attempts': 2}\nscript-analysis:reg-inf-host-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:ruby-perl-pack-reps {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:source-encoding-normalize {'ok': True, 'attempts': 2}\nscript-analysis:v3-next-lang-fixture-battery {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:v3-peel-widen {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:vba-module-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 2}\nscript-analysis:wsh-script-encoder-decode {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:xslt-msxsl-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:yaml-ci-host-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\n2026-10-17 22:30:03.522071189 +0800","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be6da17f-235a-4ec9-aa50-77364f254ac2","uuid":"516064b3-dff5-41a0-b89d-807a172b5aa6","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:08:37.113Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): source-encoding-normalize, equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route. Resolved: mastery-runner-budget (D17 5-set Mastery 12.7 s).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"network-evidence-indicators\", \"concept\": \"extract fetch indicators from network evidence (pcap/pcapng, HAR, Zeek/proxy/DNS logs, Sysmon EID 3/22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 'Fetch Quest' prompt: 'the generated network evidence says where the requests actually went' -- not shipped yet, the likeliest next twist. Pure-python module network_indicators(path)->[{kind: http|dns|tls|conn, host, url, ip, port, src_member}] sniffing by magic/shape: pcap D4C3B2A1/A1B2C3D4, pcapng 0A0D0D0A (dpkt in .venv; tshark INSTALLED as oracle: `tshark -r f -T fields -e http.host -e http.request.uri -e dns.qry.name -e tls.handshake.extensions_server_name`), HAR JSON log.entries[].request.url, Zeek TSV `#fields` header (http.log host+uri, dns.log query, ssl.log server_name), squid/proxy CSV, EVTX-exported Sysmon JSON (DestinationHostname, QueryName). Never contact any host. Fixtures: synthetic pcap/HAR/log built from today's 127 decoded plan urls with a few added/removed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"network-evidence-reconcile\", \"concept\": \"reconcile source-declared fetch targets vs observed network evidence; the one-sided indicator\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'reconcile both into one download graph, and find the indicator that shows up on only one side of the story'. Given decoded plans (url, upload_url, next_stage, host_id) for every member and network_indicators() output, canonicalise both sides (indicator-refang-normalize), return {declared_only, observed_only, both} at host and full-URL level plus the member each declared url came from. Answer kinds: exact_text (the one-sided url/host), enum of member names (which file's fetch never happened), integer (count). Depends on network-evidence-indicators.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"download-graph-model\", \"concept\": \"build the cross-file download/handoff graph from decoded plans\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Title base 'download-graph'. Nodes = members, urls, file_paths, next_language/next_stage targets; edges member->url (acquire_remote/http_client), url->file_path (write_file), member->next_language (handoff). Expose graph queries for likely question shapes: ordered_tokens chain (follow next_language/next_stage across files, '>'-joined), integer counts (distinct hosts, edges, stages), enum (member whose url/file_path is unique, root/leaf of the chain). Data already in every v=1/v=2/v=3 plan; no new decoding.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"plan-key-passthrough\", \"concept\": \"answer a question on ANY plan key without code change\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"v=3 plans carry keys never asked so far (`verdict=benign|suspicious` since D16; `language`). Generic resolver: answer-id field suffix (longest match, hyphens->underscores) -> plan key, with aliases campaign->campaign_id, file-path->file_path, upload-url->upload_url; ordered_tokens -> '>'-join of comma lists; enum -> verify against accepted_values. Gate: every D8-D17 v=3 id still answers identically; a synthetic `<family>-verdict` / `-language` question answers plan-verbatim.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"indicator-refang-normalize\", \"concept\": \"canonical URL/host comparison (defang, case, ports, punycode, underscores)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Network/report evidence is often defanged (hxxp, [.], (.), [:]//, {dot}); hosts like `auto_hotkey-<10hex>.example.invalid` contain underscores that strict URL parsers reject. canon_url(s)/canon_host(s): refang, lowercase scheme+host, IDNA punycode<->unicode, drop default port/fragment/trailing '/', percent-decode unreserved, keep path case. Return the ORIGINAL spelling for answers (exact_text is verbatim), use canon only for matching.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vba-module-route\", \"concept\": \"VBA modules (.bas/.cls, vbaProject.bin MS-OVBA compressed source)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"4th WSH-family language never polyglotted. Check what container-carrier-extract emits for vbaProject.bin; add pure-python MS-OVBA decompression (dir stream -> module offsets) if missing, then Codec_/marker scan. Oracle: .venv/bin/olevba --decode. (1st prebuild attempt failed D16 night -- retry.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"python-exec-onion-static\", \"concept\": \"exec(marshal/zlib/base64(..)) / lambda onions without exec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"AST walker that folds b64decode/b85decode/zlib.decompress/bytes.fromhex/[::-1]/codecs.decode(rot13) calls on literals and stops at exec/eval/marshal.loads; marshal blobs -> xdis disassembly (version from magic) to pull const strings. Replaces the old python-exec-layers note; Python is the only carried language with a carrier axis (D6 cx_Freeze). (1st prebuild attempt failed -- retry.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ahk-compiled-exe-extract\", \"concept\": \"compiled AutoHotkey/AutoIt carriers + AHK v1 legacy syntax\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 AHK and D12 AutoIt shipped source only; the D6 Python precedent (cx_Freeze on a TT) says a compiled carrier can appear on a variant. AHK Ahk2Exe stores the script as PE RCDATA `>AUTOHOTKEY SCRIPT<` / `>AHK WITH ICON<` (plain text, v1.1.34+ optionally compressed) -> pefile (.venv) resource walk; AutoIt a3x -> existing autoit-ripper / .venv/bin/a3x. Also accept AHK v1 descriptor forms: `descriptor_x = text` (unquoted legacy), `descriptor_x := \\\"..\\\"`, continuation sections `(\\\\n..\\\\n)` and `.`-concat. Route the recovered text through the V3_MARK path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dockerfile-makefile-route\", \"concept\": \"Dockerfile / Makefile build hosts\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Join `\\\\` continuations; Dockerfile `ARG/ENV DESCRIPTOR_X=..`, `RUN echo .. | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..`, TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)` (never `make -n`). Marker in `#` comments. (1st prebuild attempt failed -- retry.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..).\"}\n]\n```\nscript-analysis:ahk-compiled-exe-extract {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:batch-expansion-regime-lib {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:batch-substring-emulation {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:container-carrier-extract {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:descriptor-syntax-generic {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:dockerfile-makefile-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 2}\nscript-analysis:download-graph-model {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:equivalence-outlier-compare {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:gzip-zlib-codec-rep {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:indicator-refang-normalize {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:network-evidence-indicators {'ok': False, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:network-evidence-reconcile {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:php-eval-chain {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:plan-key-passthrough {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:ps-layer-peel {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:python-exec-onion-static {'ok': False, 'attempts': 2}\nscript-analysis:reg-inf-host-route {'ok': True, 'attempts': 1}\nscript-analysis:ruby-perl-pack-reps {'ok': T