{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BMjMnMNzd6yGaGxnbB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QjcmUpC7yASAz5s7vtVGND","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","old_string":"| Prompt about fetch targets vs \"network evidence\" / \"only one side\" (D17), but the zip holds only scripts | Flavour: answer the per-file ids. If a pcap/HAR/proxy/DNS log ever ships: list hosts+URLs on each side (`tshark -r f.pcap -T fields -e http.host -e http.request.uri -e dns.qry.name -e tls.handshake.extensions_server_name`, INSTALLED; `dpkt` in .venv), refang/lowercase both, take the symmetric difference. |","new_string":"| Prompt about fetch targets vs \"network evidence\" / \"only one side\" (D17), but the zip holds only scripts | Flavour: answer the per-file ids. If a HAR/Zeek/proxy/DNS log ships: `r = lib.codec.reconcile({member: plan}, raw_bytes)` -> `reconcile_answer(r, kind, accepted_values, what=)` (indicator / `urls.observed_only` / unfetched member / counts; refang + canon via `canon_url`/`canon_host`, answers keep the ORIGINAL spelling). Raw pcap is NOT parsed by lib yet: `tshark -r f -T fields -e http.host -e http.request.uri -e dns.qry.name -e tls.handshake.extensions_server_name` (INSTALLED) and pass the lines in as text. Graph questions (chain / root / leaf / unique host / counts): `lib.codec.download_graph(plans)` + `download_graph_answer`. |\n| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before (`-verdict`, `-language`, ...) | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore, aliases). Copy plan-verbatim. |"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2871,"cache_read_input_tokens":90913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"eph