{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8BRaf1QSkUWrByT3ymv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VXto1jQupdSsJ1SKm6gWyM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nhead,gaps=s[:i],s[i:]\nm=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',gaps,re.S)\nold=json.loads(m.group(1))\nbuilt={'download-graph-model','network-evidence-reconcile','plan-key-passthrough','indicator-refang-normalize',\n       'ahk-compiled-exe-extract','vba-module-route','dockerfile-makefile-route','python-exec-onion-static'}\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in old if g['id'] not in built}\nnei=keep['network-evidence-indicators']\nnei['detail']=(\"RETRY (1st attempt D17 night reverted: `import csv` is outside the prebuild gate's allowlist -- hand-split TSV/CSV \"\n \"with re/str.split, quotes via a small regex). D17 prompt: 'the generated network evidence says where the requests actually went'. \"\n \"network_indicators(data, name='')->[{kind: http|dns|tls|conn, host, url, ip, port, method, user_agent, src}] sniffing by magic/shape: \"\n \"pcap D4C3B2A1/A1B2C3D4 and pcapng 0A0D0D0A via dpkt (allowed) or struct -- HTTP request line + Host, DNS qname (+A/CNAME answers), \"\n \"TLS ClientHello SNI, TCP SYN dst ip:port; feed the list straight into lib.codec.observed_fetches()/reconcile(). \"\n \"tshark (INSTALLED) is the test oracle only. Fixtures: synthetic pcap/pcapng built with struct from today's decoded plan urls, \"\n \"one url added and one removed.\")\nnew=[\n nei,\n {\"id\":\"source-fetch-sites\",\"concept\":\"declared fetch targets read from the CODE (download cradles), not only the plan\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D17 prompt: 'the source code says where it would fetch from'. If a fixture's code and plan disagree (or a member has no plan url), the declared side must come from call sites. fetch_sites(src, name='')->[{api, url, method, line}] for PS Invoke-WebRequest/iwr/irm/Net.WebClient.DownloadString|DownloadFile|UploadString/Start-BitsTransfer, certutil -urlcache -split -f, bitsadmin /transfer, curl/wget/Invoke-RestMethod, mshta http.., regsvr32 /i:http, JS/VBS/VBA MSXML2.XMLHTTP|ServerXMLHTTP|WinHttp .open, Node fetch/http(s).get/axios, Python urllib.request.urlopen/requests.get|post, Ruby Net::HTTP/URI.open, Perl LWP get/HTTP::Tiny, PHP file_get_contents/curl_init, Lua socket.http/ngx.location.capture, AHK Download()/WinHttpRequest, AutoIt InetGet/InetRead, AppleScript do shell script \\\"curl. Rebuild URLs from '+'/'&'/'.'/'..' concat, -f format, join() and char-code arrays over the file's own literals (re only; no ast/eval). Gate: on the D17 bundle every v=1/v=2/v=3 member's fetch_sites url equals (or is absent from) its plan url.\"},\n {\"id\":\"reconcile-indicator-kinds\",\"concept\":\"one-sided indicators that are not URLs (IP, user agent, file name, port, JA3)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"lib.codec.reconcile compares urls/hosts only. Extend the report with ips (conn dst / DNS A answers), user_agents (HAR request headers, Zeek http user_agent, PS sample UA indicator), file_names (URI basename, Content-Disposition, plan file_path/next_stage basename), ports; same {declared_only, observed_only, both} shape and reconcile_answer(what='user_agents.observed_only' ...). The question 'which indicator shows up on only one side' may name any indicator kind the lane already extracts (url, wallet, mutex, UA, file).\"},\n {\"id\":\"http-redirect-dns-resolve\",\"concept\":\"follow redirects / DNS CNAME+A so declared and observed sides join\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"'Where the requests actually went' can differ by a 30x Location hop or a CNAME. From HAR (response.redirectURL / Location header / status), pcap HTTP responses and DNS answers build host->ip and url->final_url maps; reconcile() should count a declared url as fetched when its redirect chain or resolved IP appears, and report the redirect target as the observed-only value. Expose resolve_chain(observed)->{url: [hops]}.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pcap-http-object-hashes\",\"concept\":\"reassemble HTTP bodies from pcap -> name/size/sha256/next-stage decode\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Depends on network-evidence-indicators. dpkt TCP reassembly by (flow, seq) for port-80 / plain HTTP, Content-Length and chunked transfer-encoding, gzip Content-Encoding -> [{uri, status, content_type, size, sha256, body}]. Bodies that are scripts go back through find_codecs / the V3 marker peel (the fetched next stage). Questions likely: sha256 of the downloaded payload, its file name, its decoded plan values.\"},\n {\"id\":\"sysmon-proxy-log-fetches\",\"concept\":\"observed network side from Sysmon / proxy / web-server logs\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"observed_fetches() covers HAR, Zeek TSV and free text. Add: Sysmon EID 3 (DestinationHostname/DestinationIp/Port, Image) and EID 22 (QueryName, QueryResults, Image) from EVTX (Evtx lib allowed) or exported XML/JSON; IIS/W3C `#Fields:` logs; Apache/nginx combined; squid native access.log (`ts elapsed client code/status bytes METHOD URL`). Keep the Image/process so an 'only one side' answer can name the process that fetched. No csv module (gate): split by regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ps-v3-polyglot-route\",\"concept\":\"PowerShell as a v=3 polyglot (.ps1/.psm1/.psd1/.ps1xml)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"PS is the only D1 language with no v=3 fixture; a polyglot-powershell day would put the marker in `<# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:.. #>` block comments or `#` lines and the descriptor in `$descriptor_x = '..'`, `[string]$descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"`, here-strings `@' .. '@` / `@\\\" .. \\\"@`, or a `.psd1` hashtable `Descriptor = '..'`. Ensure the lib marker/descriptor helpers accept all of these and that an is_v3(src) check exists so callers route v=3 before the v=1 `$encodedMaterial`/`$nativeTypes` JSON path. Fixture battery: carried D17 polyglot plans re-wrapped in each PS form.\"},\n {\"id\":\"lolbin-download-attack-table\",\"concept\":\"fetch API / LOLBin -> ATT&CK + adapter label table\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Data table in lib.scripts used by source-fetch-sites: certutil T1105 (+T1140 when -decode), bitsadmin/Start-BitsTransfer T1197, mshta T1218.005, regsvr32 /i T1218.010, rundll32 T1218.011, msiexec /i http T1218.007, curl/wget/IWR/WebClient/XMLHTTP/fetch T1105, upload verbs T1041/T1567. Remember the lane's GM history: plans' attack= wins; this table only fills ids with no plan value, return candidates in order.\"},\n {\"id\":\"python-onion-regex-fold\",\"concept\":\"Python exec onions folded without ast/marshal\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Replaces python-exec-onion-static (given up after 2 attempts: `import ast` is outside the gate allowlist). Regex-fold literal call chains innermost-first with base64/zlib/codecs/binascii only: b64decode/b32decode/b85decode, zlib.decompress, bytes.fromhex, codecs.decode(..,'rot13'), [::-1], .decode(); stop at exec/eval/marshal.loads and return the last literal. marshal blobs: report only (xdis not in the allowlist).\"},\n]\nrest=[g for gid,g in keep.items() if gid!='network-evidence-indicators']\nallg=new+rest\nfor g in allg: assert set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'},g['id']\nids=[g['id'] for g in allg]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nfor g in new[1:]: assert 'script-analysis:'+g['id'] not in st, g['id']\nbody=\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in allg)\nline=(\"Built by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16 night source-encoding-normalize, \"\n \"equivalence-outlier-compare, batch-expansion-regime-lib, v3-next-lang-fixture-battery, wsh-script-encoder-decode, ruby-perl-pack-reps, \"\n \"yaml-ci-host-route, reg-inf-host-route; D17 night download-graph-model, network-evidence-reconcile, plan-key-passthrough, \"\n \"indicator-refang-normalize, ahk-compiled-exe-extract, vba-module-route, dockerfile-makefile-route (all `lib.codec`). Given up: \"\n \"python-exec-onion-static (2 attempts, `import ast` banned -> replaced by python-onion-regex-fold). Prebuild gate: lib imports \"\n \"limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (no csv/ast/tokenize/shlex/marshal; dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile OK). Resolved: \"\n \"mastery-runner-budget (D17 5-set Mastery 12.7 s).\")\nnewgaps=\"## Readiness gaps\\n\"+line+\"\\n\\n```json\\n[\\n\"+body+\"\\n]\\n```\\n\"\ns=head+newgaps\njson.loads(re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',s,re.S).group(1))\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\npending=[g['id'] for g in allg if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('script-analysis:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pending),pending)\nEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2008,"cache_read_input_tokens":98373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2008},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be6da17f-235a-4ec9-aa50-77364f254ac2","uuid":"87cbd012-23bf-4516-b396-382cfd38d6e2","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:11:39.894Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8BRaFTX6hXBdDZDKHHC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VXto1jQupdSsJ1SKm6gWyM":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nhead,gaps=s[:i],s[